<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Hand-trimmed fixture standing in for Google-Chrome-2.11, the latest revision PowerStig ships of
  the Chrome STIG (#103's map). Rule ids, field values and dscresourcemodule attributes are copied
  from the real processed data in the local PowerStig clone rather than invented, trimmed the way
  the WindowsClient and WindowsServer fixtures are (short Description, no VulnDiscussion/RawString
  prose).

  Chrome carries only two rule types: Registry (45 rules, 43 RegistryPolicyFile and 2 Registry
  dscresource) and Manual (1 rule, produces nothing) - both already proven by every prior Windows
  map, so this fixture is a survey rather than new generator work. V-221558 is an ordinary
  RegistryPolicyFile rule; V-221563 is the real Registry rule whose value the organisation
  decides; V-221572 is the Registry dscresource variant. Unlike WindowsClient's real data, no
  Chrome rule id carries an .a/.b sub-rule pair.
-->
